---
import PhotoPlaceholder from '../PhotoPlaceholder.astro';
---

<section>
  <!-- Panel 1: full-viewport dark hero. The id + view-timeline-name are set
       here directly (rather than via the inline-style loop in vision.astro)
       because Frame doesn't use SectionHead and we need the timeline on the
       hero panel specifically — not the outer <section> that also wraps the
       prose panel below the fold. -->
  <div
    id="intro"
    class="frame-hero band-ink"
    style="view-timeline-name: --tl-intro; view-timeline-axis: block;"
  >
    <PhotoPlaceholder
      fill
      variant="ink"
      description="Hero image — a Las Vegas streetscape in the won state. Shaded sidewalk, BRT bus pulling up, kids on bikes, the Spring Mountains beyond. Full-bleed, generous breathing room."
    />
    <div class="frame-hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="frame-hero__text">
      <h1 class="frame-heading">This is the Las&nbsp;Vegas Valley we're building.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        A neighborhood where you walk to the store. A household that doesn't spend a quarter of its
        income on cars. A high-school kid who gets home from practice without calling for a ride.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="frame-scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">scroll ↓</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Panel 2: below-fold prose -->
  <div class="band-cream section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="vision-prose">
        <p>
          Streets where we stop killing people with the way we drew the lines. Schools and parks and
          groceries inside a five-minute walk. A bus that comes often enough that you stop checking
          the schedule. That's the concrete part.
        </p>
        <p>
          A Valley people feel proud to live in, not just tolerant of. Transit that isn't something
          you apologize for using. A Las&nbsp;Vegas that people move <em>to</em>, not just through.
          That's the part the spreadsheet won't show you, and it matters as much.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
